/target/
*.obj

# Tauri regenerates these on every build from tauri.conf.json
/crates/evmedia-gui/gen/

# Script output. A rule earns its place here only while its producer writes something that must
# not be committed -- ticket 03 deleted the scripts that wrote `strings_dump.txt`,
# `found_segments.txt`, `capture_error.txt`, `evplayer2_manifest.json`, `decoded.ts` and
# `decoded.mp4`, so their rules went with them and this list is now producer-backed.
#
# capture_all.py output (contains session tokens, JWT, tk, sign - do not commit)
tools/parser-tools/captured/
tools/parser-tools/ev2_out/
tools/parser-tools/urls.log
tools/parser-tools/ctx_dump.json
tools/parser-tools/triple.json
# A redis dump holding every segment's key and XOR mask for a whole lesson -- the recovered
# credential class itself, and not ours to redistribute.
tools/parser-tools/EVPlayer2_解密工具与参数/redis_segments.json
# A recorded context dump kept as evidence. No script writes it any more, but it is a memory dump
# and must stay out of the repository regardless.
tools/parser-tools/dump_contexts.json

rust_out/
# Same thing under the name a later run used; the pattern is the reason, not the name.
rust_out_today/
# Ghidra's own source tree, downloaded to read when the MCP server is not running. Not ours, and
# far too large to belong in this repository.
ghidra-master/
# The output directories ticket 02's verification runs use -- `verify_out/`, `verify_out2/`,
# `verify_out3/`, one per grab run. Run output, never a source file, and the `*` is the point:
# a rule pinned to one name lets the next run's directory straight into the index.
verify_out*/
# The desktop window's own verification root: a sniffed `session.json` (a bearer token), the
# catalog the CLI wrote, and whatever it exported. A credential, so it stays out by rule rather
# than by remembering.
/verify_fresh/
/verify_gui/

# Poster output: the compiled generator and what running it leaves behind. `build/Poster.cs` is the
# source and is tracked; these are build products.
/build/Poster.exe
/build/frames/
/build/*.png

.idea
.vscode
__pycache__/

# tools/export_video.py complete video output
/ev-videos/
